    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **261 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS** \u2014 including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesAgeBand`, all JDBC/JPA repository tests (which exercise the new `birth_date` column across HSQLDB and H2), and the pre-existing owner/pet/vet controller tests.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe request may carry an ISO `birthDate`; the response derives an `ageBand` relative to `registrationDate`. Since `ageBand` is a **read-time derived field** (like `locality`, `contactPreference`, `checkDigit`) and `birthDate` is a normal editable owner field that flows through the existing MapStruct-based create pipeline, no new OfficeFloor endpoint or YAML wiring was needed \u2014 the create pipeline already maps the full `OwnerFieldsDto` into the entity.\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (ISO date, optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only `ageBand` string to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain both fields.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persistent `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, column `birth_date`) with getter/setter, so it round-trips POST \u2192 DB \u2192 GET.\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a nullable `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `ageBand` via a new `ageBand(owner)` method: `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` \u2192 `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+); returns `null` (field omitted) when `birthDate` is absent.\n\n`birthDate` binds in the request via the existing `ValidateOwner`/`BuildOwner` MapStruct mapping (by name), so it's persisted at create and available when `GET /api/owners/{id}` computes `ageBand`.",
